WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.400
-Welcome.
You and I go way back,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.701
and I just want
to tell this story just so that

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:09.767
you know how much I think about
you and speak about you a lot.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:14.200
I was a stand-up comedian,
and it was probably 1996 or '97.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.033
-'97, yeah.
-It was before I was on

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.667
"Saturday Night Live."
I was doing stand-up.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.534
I got a gig to open for you

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.534
at the Universal Amphitheater
in Los Angeles.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:22.901
-Yep.
-And so I went.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:26.267
I said hi to you and Davy.
But you said to me --

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.000
You go,
"Hey, what's your name again?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.167
It was Jimmy?"
I go, "Yeah."

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.200
You go, "I think you got
something there, kid."

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.868
-Yeah.
-And I go -- and I go,

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.300
"Oh, thank you so much."
I'm freaking out meeting you.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.334
And you go, "I'm actually
directing this pilot.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.501
If you want to audition,
have your manager

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.834
call this guy
you're working with."

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.334
-Yeah.
-And you gave me an audition.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.434
I don't know
if the show went anywhere.

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.834
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.734
-I wanted to tell you,
it built my confidence

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:51.033
as a comedian and someone who
couldn't get a gig

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.767
or get a callback or anything.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.701
That little boost,
that little

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.367
someone believing in you
really meant a lot to me.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.267
-Oh, thank you.
-And I'll never forget it,

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.634
and I really thank you so much.
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:04.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You're a good man.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.634
And I was freaking out
because there's another

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.901
famous Jimi
who opened for you, as well.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.300
This is a famous --
do you know -- funny story.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah, this is --

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.501
if you look right here,

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.133
Jimi Hendrix
opened for you guys.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.467
-Yeah.
-What was Jimi Hendrix like?

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.000
-Wonderful, wonderful guy.
I was in New York,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
and I was -- earlier on,
before he was Jimi Hendrix.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.801
And somebody said, "You gotta
go down to the Cafe Au Go Go,

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.334
see this guitar player who's
playing with

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.133
John Hammond's band."

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.567
I went down there,
and sure enough --

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.501
And they said he was known
as this guy

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.534
that plays guitar
with his teeth.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.667
We were looking
for an opening act.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.968
And I suggested them,
opening for the headlining act

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:48.767
can be a problem sometimes
for the opening act.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:51.300
Well, it was -- I'm not kidding.
It was --

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.100
♪ Purple haze come in my brain ♪

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.601
-Yeah, yeah.
-"We want Davy!

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:57.934
We want The Monkees!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.801
-Yeah, "We want The Monkees."

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.434
-♪ Foxy lady ♪
"Micky!"

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.267
-"Dolenz!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.534
-Terrible nightmare
for Jimi Hendrix.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.133
-Oh, it was embarrassing.
-You have so many stories,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.834
and you actually
have an announcement

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.334
that you're gonna make tonight.
You're actually --

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.033
These photos that you have
throughout all the years,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.634
you're finally publishing them.
-Yep.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.834
A book that is called --
[ Applause ]

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:22.033
-It's a big deal.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:26.033
-A book coming out
in November called

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:27.767
"I'm Told I Had a Good Time."

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:32.200
-That is
a great title right there.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.334
That is fantastic.
"I'm Told --"

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:36.801
-So true.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.000
-I'd kick myself
if I didn't ask.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.067
'Cause I know
you're going on tour.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.767
You're about to play --

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:44.067
You're celebrating The Monkees.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:47.100
-But I would kick myself
if I didn't ask if you would

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.601
like to --
Can you sing something?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.334
-Oh, I'd love to.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:52.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.501
I'd love to.
I'm sorry.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:58.133
I can't, 'cause I need a
tambourine to sing, and I --

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.834
[ Tambourine rattling ]

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:04.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.400
-Micky Dolenz,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.300
"Last Train to Clarksville."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:18.067
♪♪

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:20.834
♪ Take the last train
to Clarksville ♪

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.267
♪ I'll meet you at the station ♪

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.834
♪ You can be here by 4:30 ♪

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.067
